    "description": "<p>The world of data modelling, publishing and sharing has changed rapidly in the last years. Starting from the invention of<br>\nthe World Wide Web in 1989 by Sir Tim Berners-Lee this Web is on an evolution to the so called Web 4.0. Before we will<br>\nreach that we have to ll the Semantic Web as part of the Web 3.0 with resources and research content. Therefore the 5 star<br>\nopen data principles, the Linked Open Data principles, the 5 star LOUD principles and the FAIR principles are necessary. I<br>\nwill merge all of that principles in the so called Sphere 7 Data principles, described in this paper.</p>",
